{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>See that YHWH has given you the Sabbath.</b> They said in the Midrash Tehillim, on the section of the psalm מזמור שיר ליום השבת (Psalms 92:1): What is the meaning of ראו? R. Yosi said: See the precious gift that I have given you. R. Yitzhak said: Every matter of the Sabbath is doubled — the עמר is doubled, for it is written (Exodus 16:16) שני העומר לאחד — 'an omer per head'; its offering is doubled (Numbers 28:9): וביום השבת שני כבשים — 'and on the Sabbath day two lambs'; its punishment is doubled: מחלליה מות יומת — 'he who profanes it shall surely be put to death' (the expression doubled); its reward is doubled (Isaiah 58:13): וקראת לשבת עונג לקדוש ה׳ מכובד — 'and you shall call the Sabbath a delight, the holy of YHWH honored'; its admonitions are doubled: זכור — 'Remember' (Exodus 20:8) — and שמור — 'Observe' (Deuteronomy 5:12); its psalm is doubled (Psalms 92:1): מזמור שיר ליום השבת — 'A psalm, a song for the Sabbath day.' And this is what Scripture says: הבל הבלים אמר קהלת הבל הבלים הכל — 'Vanity of vanities, said Qohelet; vanity of vanities, all is vanity' (Ecclesiastes 1:2) — seven vanities. Why? Corresponding to the seven days of Creation. Solomon said: What was created on the first day? — Heaven and earth. And what is their end? (Isaiah 51:6): כי שמים כעשן נמלחו והארץ כבגד תבלה — 'For the heavens shall vanish like smoke, and the earth shall wear out like a garment.' And he said: הבל — vanity. What was created on the second day? — The firmament (רקיע). And it is written (Isaiah 34:4): ונגלו כספר השמים — 'and the heavens shall be rolled together like a scroll.' And he said: הבל. What was created on the third day? — The gathering of the waters (יקוו המים). What is their end? (Isaiah 11:15): והחרים ה׳ לשון ים מצרים — 'and YHWH shall utterly destroy the tongue of the Egyptian sea.' And he said: הבל. What was created on the fourth day? — The lights (יהי מאורות). And what is their end? (Isaiah 24:23): וחפרה הלבנה ובושה החמה — 'and the moon shall be confounded, and the sun ashamed.' And he said: הבל. What was created on the fifth day? — Swarming creatures and birds (שרץ ועוף), as stated (Genesis 1:20): נפש חיה ועוף יעופף — 'moving creatures that have life, and birds that fly.' What is their end? (Zephaniah 1:2–3): אסוף אסף כל מעל פני האדמה אסוף עוף השמים וגו׳ — 'I will utterly sweep away all from the face of the earth; I will sweep away the birds of the sky,' etc. And he said: הבל. What was created on the sixth day? — Man (אדם). And what is his end? (Genesis 3:19): כי עפר אתה ואל עפר תשוב — 'for you are dust, and to dust you shall return.' And he said: הבל. What was created on the seventh day? — The Sabbath (שבת). He turned and examined it this way and that, to find a flaw in it, and could find none, because it is entirely holiness and rest. Said R. Yitzhak: After examining it, he saw that when a person sins regarding it, he becomes liable with his life — and he said: הבל. Therefore the all — הכל — here is one."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The printed text ends 'הרי ז׳' — abbreviated; rendered as 'here is one,' i.e., this final הבל is a single one. The prooftext from Exodus 16:16 is implicit in the source and supplied for clarity. The ending is textually compressed and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:24.184614753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}